{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfboP8F3iXjc5T7aJW3EZ", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's a regex that matches an ISO 8601 calendar date (`YYYY-MM-DD`) and checks that the month and day are in range:\n\n```\n\\b\\d{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])\\b\n```\n\n- `\\d{4}` matches the four-digit year.\n- `(0[1-9]|1[0-2])` matches months 01\u201312.\n- `(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])` matches days 01\u201331.\n- `\\b` keeps it from matching inside longer digit strings.\n\nIt matches `2026-10-01`. It won't reject impossible dates such as `2026-02-31`. Regex can't check month lengths or leap years, so validate those with a date library if you need to.\n\nFor a whole-string check, such as validating a field, swap the `\\b` anchors for `^` and `$`:\n\n```\n^\\d{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])$\n```"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7226, "cache_read_input_tokens": 16780, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7226}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "62824b82-c5ae-48b7-b1f4-219dbc8949d5", "uuid": "9814f77a-9ade-43e8-be06-95279bc2cc67", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T16:03:53.918Z", "request_id": "req_011CfboP7uhgHtjnGcDMX5Ea"}
